+# Sources consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14.
+
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation Installer API Reference Guide 9.1.0.0** —
+  https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/tree/9.1.0.0 — accessed 2026-08-14; confirmed the tagged
+  installer API release and the `SddcSpec` fields used by the greenfield artifact.
+- **Minimum number of ESXi hosts required on vSAN clusters for deployment of
+  VCF Management Domain** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/392993 — accessed 2026-08-14;
+  confirmed four hosts for a standard management domain and eight hosts, four
+  per site, for a stretched management domain.
+- **Considerations for Implementing vSphere Metro Storage Cluster on VCF 9.x** —
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/417356 — accessed 2026-08-14; confirmed that the
+  stated 4 ms RTT is inside the supported inter-site latency bound.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere
+  Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630 — accessed 2026-08-14;
+  confirmed that VCF Operations is upgraded first for a 5.2.x estate, that VCF
+  Management Services are mandatory for VCF 9.1, and the documented Automation,
+  identity, and log-management transitions.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation - Upgrade Bundle Details** —
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/327207 — accessed 2026-08-14; confirmed the pinned
+  VCF 5.2.2 SDDC Manager, vCenter, ESXi, and NSX source bundle versions.
+- **Upgrade failure for vCenter 8.0 U3j, ESXi 8.0 U3j, and NSX 4.2.4 due to
+  back-in-time restriction** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/448135 — accessed 2026-08-14;
+  confirmed the VCF 9.1.0.0 component builds and the gate against upgrading to
+  an older chronological build.
+- **Upgrade Guidance for Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for
+  Logs 9.0.x** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314 — accessed 2026-08-14;
+  confirmed that the Logs transition is side-by-side rather than in-place.
